# The Flentrop of 1958, Adolphus Busch Hall: a stop
# for dacvoice (voices/README.md, "Stops"). The division's lines (n,
# frame, envelope, chiff) are the same in each of its stops, so they mix.
name Valkfluit 2
family Hoofdwerk
n 10
frame 8
start 18 dB
attack 0.012 s
peak 0 dB
decay 0 dB/s
sustain 0 dB
release 0.05 s
chiff 0.012 s 16 dB 2 16
# Hoofdwerk: an open flute at 2 feet. Its harmonics and its level are
# measured from the opening of Biggs's recording of the Little Fugue, with
# the Roerfluit 8.
harmonics 1 1.0  2 0.085  3 0.03  4 0.012  5 0.006
rank 4 1.0
level 0 dB
# The voicing (voices/README.md, "The voicing"): the speech by the pipe's
# size, and Busch Hall, where the organ stands.
rise 10
room busch
# The celeste: a second read of the table at half the rate, 2 cents
# sharp, a rank a little off the unison.
celeste 2
